<title>USA: USDA broadens GSM-102 export credit list to Latvia.</title>
<headline>USDA broadens GSM-102 export credit list to Latvia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday it had lenthened the list of commodities available to Latvia through its GSM-102 export credit guarantee program.</p>
<p>No change was made in the total of short-term credits, $6 million, available to the Eastern European nation.</p>
<p>Newly eligible were:</p>
<p>--dried fruit, including apples, figs, dates, prunes and raisins.</p>
<p>--tree nuts, including almonds, pecans, pistachios, walnuts and hazelnuts.</p>
<p>--fresh, chilled, frozen and canned fish.</p>
<p>--wine and brandy.</p>
</text>
